---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import CopyableCode from "../../components/CopyableCode.astro";
import { InsetText, WarningText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-solid";
---

<ToolingLayout title="Set up OpenCode" currentPath="/tooling/opencode">
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Set up OpenCode</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    OpenCode can run directly in your terminal, as a desktop app, or as an
    extension in VS Code. If you connect it to the AI Gateway it will give you
    access to any{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/models">
      available AI model
    </a>{" "}
    (for example, Claude or Gemini).
  </p>

  <WarningText>
    If you are using OpenCode version 1, you must update to version 2. Run{" "}
    <code class="app-code">opencode --version</code> and, if it's 1.x, follow
    these{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/opencode-update">
      instructions to update to version 2.x
    </a>
    {"."}
  </WarningText>

  <figure class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/gateway-diagram-opencode.svg"
      alt="Diagram showing OpenCode running in the command line or in a desktop environment (as an app or VS Code extension). All connect to the AI Gateway, which provides access to Claude, Gemini, GPT and other AI models."
      class="govuk-!-width-full"
    />
  </figure>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Before you start, make sure you have{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      your AI Gateway key
    </a>
    . Then, to set up OpenCode, you need to:
  </p>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#use-admin-permissions">
        Use admin permissions
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-homebrew">
        Install Homebrew
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-vs-code">
        Install VS Code
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-opencode">
        Install OpenCode and add your AI Gateway key
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#use-the-desktop-app">
        (If needed) Use the desktop app
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#connect-to-vs-code">
        Connect OpenCode to VS Code
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These steps work for most setups. If you run into issues you can't resolve,
    contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-admin-permissions">
    Use admin permissions
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You need (temporary) admin permissions to install software on your Mac.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Select the padlock icon (<strong>Local Admin Management</strong>) on the
      top menu bar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Install an app</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Start session</strong>, and enter your laptop password.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>OK</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These permissions last for 10 minutes. Select the padlock to request more
    time.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-homebrew">
    Install Homebrew
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Homebrew lets you quickly install software using the Terminal.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    To check if you have Homebrew installed, in Terminal, run:
  </p>
  <CopyableCode code="brew" />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If the command is not found, you need to install Homebrew.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">To install Homebrew, in Terminal, run:</p>
  <CopyableCode
    code={`/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"`}
  />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you get an error message (such as{" "}
    <code class="app-code">403 Forbidden</code> or{" "}
    <code class="app-code">404 Not Found</code>):
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://github.com/Homebrew/brew/releases/tag/6.0.6"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Download the Homebrew package
      </a>{" "}
      (in the <strong>Assets</strong> section, select{" "}
      <strong>Homebrew.pkg</strong>).
    </li>
    <li>
      To install Homebrew, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="sudo installer -pkg ~/Downloads/Homebrew.pkg -target /" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-vs-code">
    Install VS Code
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    VS Code is an integrated development environment which lets you connect to
    OpenCode from your code interface.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To check if you have VS Code installed, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If the command is not found, you need to install VS Code.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number" start="2">
    <li>
      To install VS Code, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="brew install --cask visual-studio-code" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-opencode">
    Install OpenCode and add your AI Gateway key
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To install OpenCode, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="brew install opencode" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To create the OpenCode configuration folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="mkdir -p ~/.config/opencode" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/opencode.json" download>
        Download the configuration file
      </a>{" "}
      for OpenCode version 2.x. To check your version, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode --version" />
    </li>
    <li>
      If you are using OpenCode version 1.x, follow these{" "}
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/opencode-update">
        instructions to update to version 2.x
      </a>
      {"."}
    </li>
    <li>
      Move the downloaded configuration file into your OpenCode configuration
      folder:
      <CopyableCode code="mv ~/Downloads/opencode.json ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <WarningText>
    You need to download the config file regularly, as we update it with the
    latest models.
  </WarningText>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m" id="opencode-add-your-key">
    Add or renew your AI Gateway key
  </h3>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Copy your AI Gateway key (
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
        how to get your key
      </a>
      ).
    </li>
    <li>
      To start OpenCode, open a new Terminal instance and run:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To connect your key, run:
      <CopyableCode code="/connect" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Search for and select <strong>i.AI Gateway</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Paste your AI Gateway key and select <strong>enter</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-the-desktop-app">
    Use the desktop app
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you use the OpenCode desktop app, make sure you have installed{" "}
    <strong>v2</strong> of the app. Older v1 versions do not understand the
    configuration format above, so your AI Gateway models will not appear.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    The desktop app, terminal and VS Code extension all connect to the same
    OpenCode service and share credentials. So you do not add your key in the
    desktop app — instead, connect your key once through the OpenCode CLI (using{" "}
    <code class="app-code">/connect</code>, as described above), and the desktop
    app will pick it up automatically.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="connect-to-vs-code">
    Connect OpenCode to VS Code
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Open the <strong>Visual Studio Code</strong> application.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select the <strong>Extensions</strong> (boxes) button in the sidebar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Search:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>OpenCode for VS Code SST</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Install</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Once the OpenCode extension is installed, the OpenCode icon (a white box)
    appears at the top of the window.
  </p>
</ToolingLayout>
